# `await o.load()`: the call is taken to have just made the promise of the async method of the class only where the lookup comes to that class for sure. Below a constructor function a statement may have laid another function under the name, or the link may not be laid yet: what the await gives is then whatever the value that was returned settles with.
# f1 = kindOf, f3 = use
